Summary:
Today’s work focused on correcting the project structure by identifying and resolving a misplacement issue with the package.json file. The file was initially located in the wrong directory, which could affect dependency management and project execution. I moved the package.json to the appropriate root folder to ensure proper configuration and alignment with the project setup. Additionally, I reviewed the overall structure to maintain consistency and avoid similar issues in the future.
Outcomes:
Through this task, I gained a better understanding of the importance of proper project structure in full-stack applications. I learned how the placement of package.json directly impacts dependency installation and script execution. This activity improved my debugging and problem-solving skills when dealing with configuration issues. Overall, it ensured smoother project setup and reinforced best practices for organizing project files.
